# Fault key_times_money (writer 6): `sum(k * m for k in ks)`, ks = int 0..3, m money, was refused LOAD-UNIT. L §4.2
# Keys as values: "In a value position a key of an integer index is an int"; L §3.2: money times an int is money.
# (0 + 1 + 2 + 3) x 1.00 = 6.00 PLN, in either order.
=== km.tally
model km
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-25
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

index ks = int 0..3

input m: money PLN

ask q: sum(k * m for k in ks)

ask q2: sum(m * k for k in ks)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  m = 1.00 "m"
=== expect
q: 6.00 PLN
  cut 2026-10-25
q2: 6.00 PLN
  cut 2026-10-25
